2026-10-20 ASK (item 1, representation fork): the ordinary rotate path cannot allocate a fresh segment at the adopt point in the present Store: segPath is keyed ONLY by logical offset; genesis already creates the empty file there; Segs.size explicitly stops at an empty file, and cover requires predecessor body-end = successor start. Merely adding one to the offset breaks logical contiguity and the zero-index origin-position check. Two recovery-safe directions require a host! flag day (every Store re-geneses): (A) distinguish segment identity from logical offset, record the chosen identity in the atomic base and traverse committed identities; this preserves logical records but changes header/base codecs and the file reader. (B) record adoption as a durable checkpoint transition in the logical stream, then rotate after that frame; this preserves offset-based filenames but changes the replay algebra and its trust boundary. Recommend A: adoption is a received base, not an admitted record. PRICE PREMISES: no landed theorem has yet been changed; A can preserve sealed_opens / seal_facts statements over logical readers, while new physical-to-logical correspondence must account for segment identity. B requires restating the replay/fold theorems to distinguish trusted adoption from admitted history. Per the explicit design-fork pause rule, neither representation is being implemented pending ROOT's choice; item 2 continues independently. The original crash-window probe and its REAL four-line result remain at logs/CX-HOST-probe.
