Commit:     ember arlynx <tobb@ember.software>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 04:58:29 2026 -0400

    host!: publish adopted bases through fresh segment identities (HOST-71)
    
    Separate physical identity from logical offset. The authenticated atomic base
    selects a segment generation; adoption creates its header under a fresh identity
    and retains its logical offset as the new run start. An interruption before
    publication leaves the previous base and every file it selects unchanged.
    Normal seals and rotations preserve the selected generation and headerFault.
    
    Live tails refuse foreignSegment when the base generation changes. Readers reject
    missing selected identities by filename and authenticated header/name mismatches
    by foreignSegment. The physical reader and directory allocator have named proofs;
    the genesis-to-writer invariant and interrupted-open theorem use the same logical
    segRead/openWith core. No landed theorem gains a hypothesis or is restated.
    sealed_opens / seal_facts remain statements over logical readers.
    
    Flag day: all Stores re-genesis, including imported and joined/followed Stores.
    Old Stores refuse shapeMismatch before World decode or identity traversal.
    Logical record/index/carry codecs are unchanged. OPS physical-format helpers,
    generated STORE.md/EXITS.md, and the HOSTING grain test consume the new layout;
    the grain helper reads the deployed host check result instead of copying a codec.
    
    CROSS-LAYER: OPS (ROOT granted the two Ops/Plants.lean helpers and the missing-file diagnostic wording in Ops/Units.lean for the HOST-71 flag day, real 10-21).
    CROSS-LAYER: OPS (ROOT granted regenerated deploy/units/STORE.md and deploy/units/EXITS.md for the HOST-71 flag day, real 10-21; ordinary generator output only).
    CROSS-LAYER: HOSTING (ROOT granted grain.rs's header/filename parse for the HOST-71 flag day, real 10-21).
    
    SIZE: Lean modules in the Host closure: physical identity wrappers and the shared checked reader.
    SIZE: Lean modules: separate deployed physical codec, proof-only image data, and correspondence proofs.
    SIZE: Lean proof-modules: physical correspondence and interrupted-publication preservation.
    SIZE: Lean lines (Host): fresh-identity adoption, pinned readers, live-tail refusal, logical memory parity, and regression plants.
    SIZE: Lean lines (Ops): unwrap authenticated base identities and use the deployed physical header width.
    SIZE: Lean lines (deployed): authenticate and select physical identities without adding a World transition to the logical record stream.
    SIZE: Lean lines (tooling: Sim, Rows, Journey, Census, Emit, Ops, Bench): real interrupted-adoption, identity, wrapper, tail, and retained-start plants.
